-- title:
--   k-level supersingular charts, nodes and Drinfeld inertia at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the symbol $\kappa$ denotes its residue field `ResidueField A`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring; `P.ord` is its normalised valuation, `P.IsRational` says that $K\to$ `P.ResidueField` is surjective, and `P.evalAt f` is the element of $K$ representing the residue of $f$ when $f$ is $P$-integral (and $0$ otherwise). `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` is the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $M'$, `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` its coefficientwise base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` the field $\kappa(\,$`jqModC`$,\,$`jqNModC`$\,)$, and `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')` the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of the $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups provided by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses.** *(Level data.)* A prime $q$ with `hq2 : q = 2`; a non-zero $M'$ with `hqM' : ¬ q ∣ M'`; a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$ (this binding is later shadowed by a second prime also called $\ell$).
--
--   *(The supersingular place and its Gauss reduction.)* A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ with `hW` saying that $W$ consists exactly of the places in `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. those satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ`; a chosen $s\in W$; the inclusion `hle : modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the base-changed field, a surjective residue map to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue field, admitting scalings with non-zero residue, together with a degree- and divisor-preserving map on places); and `hR₀`, saying that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of that series.
--
--   *(Small field of constants.)* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$ (`hκ`).
--
--   *(Roots of unity and a tame uniformiser in $k_0$.)* A prime $\ell$ (the second binding) with $3\le \ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *(Layers.)* A type $\iota$ and a family $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`); valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $A_n=A\cap K_n$ (`hAn`); an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$ (`hn₀`); and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$.
--
--   *(Tame parameter and inertia.)* An element $\pi_t\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi_t\in A$; `htame`, saying that every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$) with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise; and `hk₀stab`, saying that every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $x\in A\leftrightarrow \tau x\in A$ maps $k_0$ into itself.
--
--   **Conclusion.** With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'`$/k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the following nine assertions hold.
--
--   (C1) $F_0$ together with the geometric constants generates everything: $k_0(\mathrm{range}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`$))\sqcup F_0=\top$.
--
--   (C2) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (C3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (C4) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (C5) There is $t\in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$: if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ lying in the maximal ideal.
--
--   (C6) (Gauss compatibility with $R_0$ at $s$.) For every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $g$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that image and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (C7) (Level equivariance.) For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (an index for the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (C8) (Smooth-point packages and the Drinfeld identification.) For every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers`, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and $\kappa$, admitting scalings with non-zero residue), such that `R.integers` meets $F_0$ exactly in $W_0$, the following three things hold.
--
--   (C8a) For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ (via `GaloisField q 2`) for which [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ with [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\,$`CoordRing q κ`$)$ of the subgroup generated by the actions of the pairs $(1,\zeta)$, $\zeta\in C_s$), with $\#C_s=$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (that is, `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`), and such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ for which `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and for which $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of `hChar q`), the automorphism of $\mathrm{FSS}$ induced on residues by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` corresponds under $e$ to the action of that pair through [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16).
--
--   (C8b) For every ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbb{F}_{q^2}\to\kappa$, used as the algebra structure, for which [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ with $\#C_s=$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` there are $\eta\in\{1,q\}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ with `quotField q κ Cs` satisfying, first, the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance as in (C8a), and second, the following compatibility with tame inertia: for every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` and every unit $\alpha$ of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ with $\iota(\alpha)=$ `A.tameCharacter πt τ`, and for the semilinear automorphism $g$ of `fieldBar q M'` equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54), the map $g$ preserves `R.integers`, and for every ring automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ inducing $g$ on $R$-residues, every unit $d$ of $\mathbb{Z}/q$ with image $\alpha^{q+1}$ in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$, and every proof that the pair $(\,$`diagOneElem q (d ^ η)⁻¹`$,\alpha^{\eta})$ lies in `hSubgroup q`, the automorphism $\varphi$ corresponds under $e$ to the action of that pair through `hFunctionFieldAction`.
--
--   (C8c) There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_{Q,n}$ of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_{Q,n}:A_n[X]\to S_{Q,n}$ and $\chi_{Q,n}:S_{Q,n}\to\kappa$, and sets $D_{Q,n}$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, indexed by places $Q$ and layers $n$, with $\#N=q+1$, and:
--
--   — (affine chart) there is a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` contained in `R.integers`, contained in $S_{Q,n}$ for every $Q\notin N$ and every $n$, and such that every $z\in\mathrm{FSS}$ which is integral at all places outside $N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$;
--
--   — for every $Q\notin N$ and every layer $n$: the reduction map $A_n\to\kappa$ is surjective; the image of $A_n$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $S_{Q,n}$; $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for $a\in A_n$; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X))=0$; for every $c\in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is exactly one ring homomorphism $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_{Q,n}$ on constants, inducing $\chi_{Q,n}$ on residues, and sending $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ to $c$; every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and reduces there to the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_{Q,n}$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ is $P$-integral with `P.evalAt f` $\in A$, and such that `A.valuation (P.evalAt f)` $<1$ if and only if $\chi_{Q,n}(f)=0$; for every $\chi:S_{Q,n}\to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_{Q,n}$ on constants and inducing $\chi_{Q,n}$ on residues there is exactly one $P\in D_{Q,n}$ with `P.evalAt f` $=\chi(f)$ for all $f$; for $P\in D_{Q,n}$, an element $f$ of $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of\ }K_n)\sqcup F_0$ is $P$-integral if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in S_{Q,n}$ and `P.evalAt h` $\neq 0$; every non-zero $f$ of that subfield with $P$-order $0$ for all $P\in D_{Q,n}$ becomes a unit of $S_{Q,n}$ after multiplication by the image of a non-zero element of $K_n$; every $f$ of that subfield which lies in `R.integers` and is $P$-integral for all $P\in D_{Q,n}$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f\in S_{Q,n}$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ and the image of $A_n$, and $h$ a unit of $S_{Q,n}$;
--
--   — (layer compatibility, for $Q\notin N$) the $S_{Q,n}$ increase with $K_n$, $S_{Q,n'}$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ and the image of $A_{n'}$ whenever $K_n\le K_{n'}$, the element $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ does not depend on $n$, and $\chi_{Q,n'}$ restricts to $\chi_{Q,n}$ on $S_{Q,n}$ whenever $K_n\le K_{n'}$;
--
--   — for $Q,Q'\notin N$, any layer $n$ and any place $P$ lying in both $D_{Q,n}$ and $D_{Q',n}$, one has $Q=Q'$;
--
--   — for $Q\notin N$, every $n$ and every $P\in D_{Q,n}$, the image of `jq` in `fieldBar q M'` has non-negative $P$-order;
--
--   — for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves `R.integers`: the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ` preserves $N$ (membership is equivalent for $Q$ and for its translate), and for $Q\notin N$ and every $n$, `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` equals $D_{\,\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q,\,n}$.
--
--   (C9) (Nodes, crossing presentations, Hasse datum and covering.) For every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra and every regular prolongation $R$ as above with `R.integers` meeting $F_0$ exactly in $W_0$, there is a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$ with $\#N=q+1$, together with: fields $F_x$ indexed by places $x$, each a $\kappa$-algebra, regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $F_x$, places $b_x$ of $F_x$ over $\kappa$; subrings $C'_l\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_l$ (domains, adically complete for their maximal ideals) with elements $\pi_l$, exponents $E_l\in\mathbb{N}$ and $E_0\in\mathbb{N}$; sets $S(\mathrm{nd})$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, subrings $\mathcal{N}(\mathrm{nd})$ and layered subrings $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$, the latter local and Noetherian; and elements $c_x,c_y,c_u$ of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by places; such that:
--
--   — $C'_n$ is exactly $A\cap K_n$, the residue of $d\in C'_l$ vanishes precisely when $\varpi'_l$ divides $d$ in $C'_l$, $C'_{n_0}\subseteq C'_l$ for all $l$, $\varpi'_{n_0}\neq 0$, every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$, each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $1\le E_l$;
--
--   — every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with trivial tame character at $\pi_t$ fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; and there are $w\ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}=v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$ in $A$;
--
--   — for every $\mathrm{nd}\in N$: the places $b_{\mathrm{nd}}$, $\mathrm{nd}$ and all $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$ are rational; $\mathcal{N}(\mathrm{nd})$ consists of the elements lying in `(Rx nd).integers`, in `R.integers` and in every $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$; for $f\in\mathcal{N}(\mathrm{nd})$ and $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$, `P.evalAt f` $\in A$; the crossing relation $c_x c_y=(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}c_u$ holds; the $R_{\mathrm{nd}}$-residue of $c_x$ is $0$, the $R$-residue of $c_x$ has $\mathrm{nd}$-order $1$, the $R$-residue of $c_y$ is $0$, and the $R_{\mathrm{nd}}$-residue of $c_y$ has $b_{\mathrm{nd}}$-order $1$; for $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character, the semilinear automorphism $g=$ `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ` preserves $S(\mathrm{nd})$ and fixes $c_x$ and $c_y$; every element of `fieldBar q M'` is a quotient of two elements of some $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and also a quotient, with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficients, of a finite $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-combination of elements of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)$ by a non-zero element of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)$; and for every layer $l$: $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)\subseteq\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)\subseteq\mathcal{N}(\mathrm{nd})$; $S(\mathrm{nd})$ consists exactly of the places $P$ at which every element of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ is integral and every non-unit of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ evaluates into the maximal ideal of $A$; the image of $C'_l$ lies in $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$; every element of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ differs from the image of some element of $C'_l$ by a non-unit; any $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficients linearly independent over $C'_l$ annihilate only zero tuples of elements of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$; there is a subring $B_x\subseteq\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ containing $c_x,c_y,c_u$ such that $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$, and $B_x$ is generated by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and $c_u$ is a unit there; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $W_l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ E l)` (the quotient of $W_l[[u,v]]$ by `uvCrossingIdeal`) such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c\circ\sigma$ is the constant embedding `const`, every image of an element of $C'_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and for $f\in\mathcal{N}_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ with non-zero $R_{\mathrm{nd}}$-residue of $b_{\mathrm{nd}}$-order $n$ there is a unit $\gamma$ with $\iota_c(f)-\gamma V^n$ in the ideal generated by `const (π l)` and $U$, and symmetrically, for non-zero $R$-residue of $\mathrm{nd}$-order $n$, $\iota_c(f)-\gamma U^n$ lies in the ideal generated by `const (π l)` and $V$;
--
--   — distinct $\mathrm{nd},\mathrm{nd}'\in N$ have disjoint sets $S$;
--
--   — for $\mathrm{nd}\in N$ and $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$: for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` which has non-negative order at every place where the image of `jq` does, whose $R_0$-residue is integral at $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, the difference `P.evalAt` of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$;
--
--   — for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on places preserving $N$ such that for $\mathrm{nd}\in N$ the translate of a place by `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` lies in $S(\mathrm{nd})$ exactly when the place lies in $S(\tau_N(\mathrm{nd}))$, and the preimage of `(Rx nd).integers` under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equals `(Rx (τN nd)).integers`;
--
--   — for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving `R.integers`, and every $\mathrm{nd}\in N$: `R.resAut τ • nd` lies in $N$ and `smulDisc τ (S nd)` $=S(\,$`R.resAut τ • nd`$)$;
--
--   — for $\mathrm{nd}\in N$, the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every element of `R₀.integers` lies in `(Rx nd).integers`; and there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to $F_{\mathrm{nd}}$ carrying $R_0$-residues to $R_{\mathrm{nd}}$-residues of the corresponding images, and such that an element is integral at $s$ exactly when its $j$-image is integral at $b_{\mathrm{nd}}$;
--
--   — (Hasse datum) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC ℚ̄ q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in `fieldBar q M'` and there is $a_0\in A$ such that the difference of these two lies in `R.integers` with $R$-residue $0$, the $q$-th power of the residue of $a_0$ equals `s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')`, and there is $c'\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $c'$ times that difference lies in `R.integers` with non-zero residue and such that for every $\mathrm{nd}\in N$ the difference lies in `(Rx nd).integers` with non-zero residue and $\mathrm{nd}$-order of the $R$-residue equal to minus the $b_{\mathrm{nd}}$-order of the $R_{\mathrm{nd}}$-residue;
--
--   — (separating functions) for $x\in N$ and $y\notin N$ there is $g$ in `R.integers` $\cap\ \mathcal{N}_0(x,n_0)$ which is a non-unit of $\mathcal{N}_0(x,n_0)$, whose $R$-residue is non-zero of $y$-order $0$, and which is integral at every rational place at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order; and for $x\neq x'$ in $N$ there is $g$ lying in $\mathcal{N}_0(x,n_0)$ and in $\mathcal{N}_0(x',n_0)$ which is $c_x(x)$ times a unit in the former and a unit in the latter;
--
--   — (covering) every rational place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which specialises the $R_0$-data to $s$ (that is, for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` with non-negative order wherever the image of `jq` has, whose $R_0$-residue is integral at $s$, and every $a\in A$ with residue `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, the value `P.evalAt` of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$) either lies in $S(\mathrm{nd})$ for some $\mathrm{nd}\in N$, or lies in a residue disc: there are $Q\notin N$, a set $D$ of places and $z\in$ `fieldBar q M'` with `R.IsResidueDisc Q D z` — that is, $z$ is a disc coordinate at $Q$ (all places of $D$ rational with $z$ integral of valuation $<1$, $z\in$ `R.integers` with $Q$-order $1$ of its residue, each $c$ of valuation $<1$ attained by exactly one $P\in D$, first-order vanishing of $z-$`P.evalAt z`, and a unit principle), the residue map is computed pointwise on $D$, and degrees on $D$ add up to the order at $Q$ — with $P\in D$.
--
--   This is the constructor, in the case $q=2$ and at a rigidified auxiliary level, for the supersingular part of the stable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with level structure `levelH q M'`: over a small henselian field of constants $k_0$ it produces a level field $F_0$ with a discrete valuation $W_0$ agreeing with $A$ on $k_0$ and compatible with the level automorphisms, and then, for every regular prolongation matching $W_0$, both halves of the supersingular datum at the chosen supersingular place $s$ — the layered smooth-point packages with their affine chart and residue-disc bookkeeping, and the $q+1$ nodes with their $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi^E)$ crossing presentations, the Hasse datum on the Igusa-type coordinate and the identification of the special fibre with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve, equivariant for $\Gamma_0(M')$ and for tame inertia. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_cover_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_cover_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart).
